Hey, you guys! What's happening?

258
00:17:24,710 --> 00:17:25,960
Oh, my God.

259
00:17:26,120 --> 00:17:29,960
- What is that?     - Oh! They gave it to me at the sleep clinic.

260
00:17:30,130 --> 00:17:32,880
And it's going to help me not to snore.

261
00:17:34,170 --> 00:17:37,050
Well, are you asleep right now, Joe?

262
00:17:37,510 --> 00:17:40,090
You don't have to wear it unless you are.

263
00:17:40,260 --> 00:17:42,100
I know I don't have to.

264
00:17:42,930 --> 00:17:44,680
It tastes good.

265
00:17:46,060 --> 00:17:47,890
Plus, you look cool.

266
00:17:54,650 --> 00:17:56,240
Well, I just called Joshua.

267
00:17:56,400 --> 00:17:57,860
Oh, how'd it go?

268
00:17:58,030 --> 00:18:00,570
I did my best to convince him that I'm not...

269
00:18:00,740 --> 00:18:03,450
...some crazy girl who is dying to get married.

270
00:18:03,620 --> 00:18:06,410
- And I'm going through a hard time.     - What'd he say?

271
00:18:06,580 --> 00:18:09,250
Well, uh, his answering machine was very understanding.

272
00:18:13,460 --> 00:18:15,250
I feel blue. Ugh.

273
00:18:17,930 --> 00:18:20,340
I bet you anything he'll call you again.

274
00:18:20,510 --> 00:18:24,390
Yeah, maybe. But, you know, I don't think I even care.

275
00:18:24,850 --> 00:18:28,520
I don't think he's the one I'm sad about.

276
00:18:29,730 --> 00:18:33,560
I know I said I'm totally okay with Ross getting married.

277
00:18:33,860 --> 00:18:35,650
But as it turns out...

278
00:18:35,900 --> 00:18:39,030
...I don't think I'm handling it all that well.

279
00:18:39,450 --> 00:18:40,490
Yeah, maybe.

280
00:18:42,070 --> 00:18:44,700
And I'm just trying to figure out why.

281
00:18:44,870 --> 00:18:46,540
Any luck?

282
00:18:46,700 --> 00:18:49,250
Well, yeah. You know how Ross and I have always been...

283
00:18:49,410 --> 00:18:51,670
...on-again, off-again, on-again, off-again?

284
00:18:52,380 --> 00:18:55,710
I guess I just figured, somewhere down the road...

285
00:18:55,880 --> 00:18:57,880
...we would be on-again.

286
00:18:58,050 --> 00:18:59,380
Again.

287
00:19:00,630 --> 00:19:02,890
You know what? I think we all did.

288
00:19:04,970 --> 00:19:06,010
- Hey.     - Hey.

289
00:19:06,180 --> 00:19:07,430
Hey.

290
00:19:12,690 --> 00:19:14,860
I got us reservations for Sunday night.

291
00:19:15,020 --> 00:19:16,820
How about Ernie's at 9:00?

292
00:19:17,280 --> 00:19:20,400
Yeah, well, you, uh, better make it for three.

293
00:19:20,900 --> 00:19:24,200
See, I don't know if we're going to be hungry at 3:00.

294
00:19:27,160 --> 00:19:28,870
Three people.

295
00:19:29,040 --> 00:19:31,000
Joshua's not going to be there.

296
00:19:31,170 --> 00:19:34,880
- What happened?     - Um, well, I think he broke up with me.

297
00:19:35,920 --> 00:19:37,130
No. Why?

298
00:19:38,550 --> 00:19:41,170
Apparently, he scares easy.

299
00:19:42,010 --> 00:19:43,800
Rachel, I'm sorry.

300
00:19:43,970 --> 00:19:46,300
Eh, it's okay.

301
00:19:47,760 --> 00:19:52,730
Sometimes things don't work out the way you thought they would.

302
00:19:54,270 --> 00:19:55,690
Come here.

303
00:20:02,650 --> 00:20:05,280
Oh, hey, don't you have to go pick up Emily?

304
00:20:07,990 --> 00:20:09,490
- Are you okay?     - Yeah.

305
00:20:09,700 --> 00:20:11,450
I got my girls.

306
00:20:15,670 --> 00:20:17,040
Okay.

307
00:20:31,270 --> 00:20:33,480
Hey, you know what might cheer you up?

308
00:20:34,390 --> 00:20:35,440
What?

309
00:20:39,730 --> 00:20:40,980
I got to tell you...

310
00:20:41,150 --> 00:20:44,110
...this really does put me in a better mood.

311
00:20:45,320 --> 00:20:49,490
Ah, I wish there was a job where I could wear this all the time.

312
00:20:50,580 --> 00:20:52,500
Maybe someday there will be.

313
00:20:54,960 --> 00:20:58,500
Oh, God, that's Chandler coming by to borrow candles for his big date.

314
00:20:58,670 --> 00:21:01,050
No, Rachel, don't get it! He'll see us!

315
00:21:01,210 --> 00:21:03,760
No, yeah! The groom cannot see the bride.

316
00:21:03,920 --> 00:21:05,880
I'm not going to marry Chandler.

317
00:21:06,050 --> 00:21:08,220
Not after this!

318
00:21:09,680 --> 00:21:12,100
Okay guys, just relax.

319
00:21:17,350 --> 00:21:18,400
I do!

320
00:21:22,820 --> 00:21:25,610
- I gotta go.     - Wait, Joshua!

321
00:21:30,240 --> 00:21:33,160
Yeah, well, that ought to do it.

322
00:21:38,170 --> 00:21:41,290
Food's here. Fair enough.

323
00:21:41,460 --> 00:21:43,500
Fifteen-minute warning.

324
00:21:44,760 --> 00:21:46,420
Late.

325
00:22:00,150 --> 00:22:03,770
Dude, I am trying to sleep!

